<title>INDIA: TABLE-Increases in Indian crop support prices.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Increases in Indian crop support prices.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the increases in minimum support prices over the previous crop year announced by the Indian government on Monday.</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Increase in minimum support prices over previous crop year</p>
<p>- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>(All prices in rupees per quintal)</p>
<p>					 1997/98    1996/97   Difference</p>
<p>    Paddy     Common		   415	  380	 35</p>
<p>		  Fine		     435	  395	 40</p>
<p>		  Superfine		455	  415	 40</p>
<p>Jower, Bajra,</p>
<p>    Ragi and Maize		     360	  310	 50</p>
<p>Arhar (Tur)</p>
<p>    Moong, Urad			  900	  840	 60</p>
<p>    Groundnut (in shell)	     980	  920	 60</p>
<p>    Soybean   Yellow		   750	  700	 50</p>
<p>		  Black		    670	  620	 50</p>
<p>    Sunflower seed		   1,000	  960	 40</p>
<p>    Cotton   F-414/H-717	   1,330	1,180	150</p>
<p>		 H-4		     1,530	1,380	150</p>
<p>    Sesamum				950	  870	 80</p>
<p>    Niger seed			   800	  720	 80</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
